Subject: [PATCH] Do not fake the host in the Apple shell

The Apple shell exported the fixed-host rustc wrapper so that crate
metadata hashes would not depend on the Mac that builds. Cargo passes the
host that rustc reports to the build scripts of host crates as TARGET, so
with the wrapper every host build script believed it was building for
x86_64-unknown-linux-musl. The pure Linux derivations provide a zig-based
compiler for that name; the Apple shell has none, and host crates that
compile C fail: libz-sys hands --target=x86_64-unknown-linux-musl to
Xcode's clang ('stddef.h' file not found), and libgit2-sys selects
libgit2's Linux configuration (no member named 'st_mtim' in 'struct stat').
grin-ffi hits both through grin_util's `built` build-dependency; frostdart
and tor do not, because their host crates compile no C.

Drop the wrapper from the Apple shell. Apple reference builds then
reproduce across Macs of the same architecture and Xcode; a build from an
Intel Mac and one from an Apple Silicon Mac will differ in metadata hashes.
A compiler wrapper for the fake host was tried first from a plugin flake
(CC_x86_64_unknown_linux_musl stripping the target flags); it fixes
libz-sys but cannot fix libgit2-sys's configuration.

Verified with grin-ffi on an Apple Silicon Mac (macOS 26, Xcode 27.0.1):
all five Apple targets build through build-apple.sh, pass the leak scan
and export the expected symbols.
---
--- a/nix/cargo-library.nix
+++ b/nix/cargo-library.nix
@@ -821,9 +821,14 @@
     # No C compiler from nixpkgs: Apple targets must link with Xcode's.
     apple = pkgs.mkShellNoCC {
       packages = [ rust pkgs.jq pkgs.rsync kitBuildApple ] ++ appleExtraInputs;
-      # The same fixed host as the pure derivations, so crate metadata does
-      # not depend on the Mac that builds.
-      RUSTC_WRAPPER = rustcWrapper;
+      # No fixed-host RUSTC_WRAPPER here, unlike the pure derivations. Cargo
+      # hands the build scripts of host crates TARGET=<the host rustc
+      # reports>, and with the fake Linux host they configured and compiled
+      # their C for Linux: libz-sys passed --target=x86_64-unknown-linux-musl
+      # to Xcode's clang ('stddef.h' file not found) and libgit2-sys chose
+      # the st_mtim variant of libgit2. Any crate with C in a host dependency
+      # fails that way. Apple crate metadata hashes therefore depend on the
+      # building Mac's architecture, as they already depend on its Xcode.
       # Defaults for nix/build-apple.sh; a plugin's wrapper may override them.
       KIT_BUILD_APPLE = "${appleBuildScript}";
       # The cleaned source and the manifest, so the script runs without a
